    "site_desc": "The LBJ Grasslands is 16,800 acres of land managed by the US Forest Service under the US Department of Agriculture. There is a rich legacy of land use, ranging back to the mid-19th century. Currently, LBJ Grasslands are used for recreation and hunting, livestock grazing, and fossil fuel extraction. Ongoing ecological monitoring is performed at the site, along with prescribed burning.",
